{
  "slug": "roth-theorem-oq-03",
  "title": "Szemerédi's Theorem for 4-Term Progressions via Hypergraph Regularity",
  "phase": "OBSERVE",
  "status": "active",
  "tier": "C",
  "path": "full",
  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "\\forall \\delta > 0,\\ \\exists N_0,\\ \\forall N \\ge N_0,\\ \\forall A \\subseteq \\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z}\\ \\text{with}\\ |A| \\ge \\delta N:\\ \\exists a, d \\in \\mathbb{Z}/N\\mathbb{Z},\\ d \\ne 0,\\ \\{a, a+d, a+2d, a+3d\\} \\subseteq A.",
    "plain": "Roth's theorem guarantees three equally-spaced numbers in any dense set; this problem asks for the k=4 case of Szemerédi's theorem, guaranteeing four equally-spaced numbers a, a+d, a+2d, a+3d. Linear Fourier analysis (which powers the parent Roth proof) fails for 4-APs because sets can be quadratically structured; the modern route uses the (hyper)graph regularity method and a hypergraph removal lemma to force a 4-AP once the density is bounded below.",
    "whyMatters": [
      "First genuinely higher-order case of Szemerédi's theorem, the historical dividing line between linear Fourier analysis and higher-order (Gowers-norm) analysis.",
      "Extends the gallery from linear additive combinatorics (roth-theorem) into the regularity-method regime.",
      "Exercises Mathlib's Szemerédi-regularity infrastructure and shares its backbone with polynomial/multidimensional Szemerédi and property-testing removal lemmas."
    ]
  },
